<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Hermes Mobile | Private AI companion for Android 16</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Native Android 16 client for your own Hermes server with 1-tap QR pairing, command palette, everyday workflows, connection doctor, admin console, and signed GitHub releases.">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="../assets/favicon.svg">
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ pages_url }}en/">
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="{{ pages_url }}en/">
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="fr" href="{{ pages_url }}fr/">
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="{{ pages_url }}en/">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="Hermes Mobile">
  <meta property="og:title" content="Hermes Mobile | Private AI companion for Android 16">
  <meta property="og:description" content="Native Android workspace (API {{ min_sdk }} to {{ target_sdk }}, zero WebView, {{ release_apk_size_en }} signed APK) with QR pairing, command palette, connection doctor, and isolated multi-user profiles.">
  <meta property="og:url" content="{{ pages_url }}en/">
  <meta property="og:image" content="{{ pages_url }}assets/marketing/social-preview-en.png">
  <meta property="og:locale" content="en_US">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <meta name="twitter:title" content="Hermes Mobile | Private AI companion for Android 16">
  <meta name="twitter:description" content="Native Android companion for Hermes with QR pairing, command palette, connection doctor, and signed APK releases.">
  <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ pages_url }}assets/marketing/social-preview-en.png">
  <script>(function(){try{var q=new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('theme');var s=q==='light'||q==='dark'?q:localStorage.getItem('hermes-site-theme');var t=s==='light'||s==='dark'?s:(matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme:dark)').matches?'dark':'light');document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme',t);}catch(e){}})();</script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="topbar-inner">
      <a class="brand" href="./">
        <img class="brand-mark" src="../assets/favicon.svg" alt="" width="28" height="28">
        <span>Hermes Mobile</span>
      </a>
      <nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="./" class="is-active" aria-current="page">Overview</a>
        <a href="./docs/">Docs</a>
        <a href="./walkthrough/">Gallery</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/{{ repository }}" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
      </nav>
      <div class="nav-actions">
        <a class="lang-link" href="../fr/" data-lang-switch="fr" hreflang="fr" lang="fr" aria-label="Switch to French portal">Français</a>
        <button type="button" class="pill-btn" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false">Dark</button>
        <a class="topbar-apk" data-latest-apk href="https://github.com/{{ repository }}/releases/latest" rel="noopener">Download APK</a>
        <button type="button" class="menu-btn" data-menu-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="mobile-nav" aria-label="Toggle navigation">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M4 7h16v2H4V7zm0 4h16v2H4v-2zm0 4h16v2H4v-2z"/></svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="mobile-nav" class="mobile-drawer">
      <nav class="mobile-drawer-links" aria-label="Mobile navigation">
        <a href="./" class="is-active" aria-current="page">Overview</a>
        <a href="./docs/">Documentation</a>
        <a href="./walkthrough/">Screen gallery</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/{{ repository }}" rel="noopener">GitHub repository</a>
      </nav>
      <div class="mobile-drawer-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" data-latest-apk href="https://github.com/{{ repository }}/releases/latest" rel="noopener">Download signed APK</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="container hero-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="section-label">Android {{ min_android }} to {{ target_android }} · Zero WebView · {{ release_apk_size_en }} signed APK</span>
          <h1>A paper workspace for private AI on Android 16.</h1>
          <p class="lead">Connect directly to your own Hermes server with 1-tap QR pairing, review inline decision cards, run parallel tasks across discussions, and manage household profiles with zero telemetry.</p>
          <div class="hero-cta">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" data-latest-apk href="https://github.com/{{ repository }}/releases/latest" rel="noopener">Download signed APK</a>
            <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="./docs/">Read documentation</a>
            <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="./walkthrough/">Explore gallery</a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-note">Requires the companion server at <a href="{{ fork_url }}" rel="noopener">LLM-4-People/hermes-agent</a> for <code>/p/&lt;profile&gt;</code> isolation, single-use QR pairing, Linux Landlock sandboxing, and opaque push wakeups.</p>
        </div>

        <figure class="editorial-figure">
          <img src="../assets/marketing/hero-studio.png" width="1920" height="1080" fetchpriority="high" alt="Hermes Mobile overview showing the warm paper inline decision card, QR pairing tile, admin console summary, and live Android 16 light and dark screens">
          <figcaption>Native Android views calibrated for daylight paper and dark paper reading (WCAG-AA 4.5:1), 150% font scale, TalkBack, and adaptive tablets.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="facts-section" aria-label="Key technical facts">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="facts-grid">
          <div class="fact-card">
            <strong>{{ release_apk_size_en }}</strong>
            <span>Signed release APK size with R8 shrinking and Cosign attestation</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fact-card">
            <strong>{{ expected_fork_capabilities }} / {{ expected_fork_capabilities }}</strong>
            <span>Companion capabilities verified live in Connection doctor</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fact-card">
            <strong>1-tap QR</strong>
            <span>Single-use 5-minute pairing tickets plus built-in Admin console</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fact-card">
            <strong>0 WebView</strong>
            <span>Pure native Java views, Android Keystore AES-256-GCM vault, and Landlock server isolation</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-alt">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>Inspect live Android 16 screens in light and dark themes</h2>
          <p>Switch between verified English captures rendered directly on Android 16 (API 36), or compare both themes side by side.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="showcase-shell">
          <div class="showcase-controls">
            <div class="showcase-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Android 16 screens">
              <button type="button" class="showcase-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="true"
                data-src-light="../assets/screens/en/command-palette.png"
                data-src-dark="../assets/screens/dark/en/command-palette.png"
                data-badge="Android 16 · EN"
                data-title="Command palette (Ctrl+K)"
                data-desc="Jump straight to any native destination, recent thread, or encrypted template with accent-insensitive search inside a FLAG_SECURE overlay.">
                Command palette
              </button>
              <button type="button" class="showcase-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false"
                data-src-light="../assets/screens/en/templates.png"
                data-src-dark="../assets/screens/dark/en/templates.png"
                data-badge="Android 16 · EN"
                data-title="Everyday workflows"
                data-desc="Start from {{ curated_workflows_count }} built-in workflows or custom per-profile templates. Every choice stages an editable draft before you tap Send.">
                Workflows
              </button>
              <button type="button" class="showcase-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false"
                data-src-light="../assets/screens/en/connection-doctor.png"
                data-src-dark="../assets/screens/dark/en/connection-doctor.png"
                data-badge="Android 16 · EN"
                data-title="Connection doctor"
                data-desc="Runs 6 parallel health checks across server latency, companion capabilities, push delivery, updates, permissions, and language sync.">
                Connection doctor
              </button>
              <button type="button" class="showcase-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false"
                data-src-light="../assets/screens/en/presence-control.png"
                data-src-dark="../assets/screens/dark/en/presence-control.png"
                data-badge="Android 16 · EN"
                data-title="Presence and look"
                data-desc="All optional context sharing stays off by default with a 1-tap Turn everything off switch and instant day/night palettes.">
                Presence
              </button>
            </div>

            <div class="theme-segment" role="group" aria-label="Preview theme mode">
              <button type="button" data-stage-mode="light" aria-pressed="true">Light</button>
              <button type="button" data-stage-mode="dark" aria-pressed="false">Dark</button>
              <button type="button" data-stage-mode="both" aria-pressed="false">Both</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="stage-wrap">
            <div id="showcase-phones" class="stage-phones">
              <div class="device-frame is-phone">
                <img id="showcase-img" src="../assets/screens/en/command-palette.png" width="1080" height="2340" alt="Command palette (Ctrl+K)">
              </div>
              <div class="device-frame is-phone stage-phone-secondary">
                <img id="showcase-img-dark" src="../assets/screens/dark/en/command-palette.png" width="1080" height="2340" alt="Command palette (Ctrl+K) in dark theme" loading="lazy">
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="stage-meta">
              <span id="showcase-badge" class="badge">Android 16 · EN</span>
              <h3 id="showcase-title">Command palette (Ctrl+K)</h3>
              <p id="showcase-desc">Jump straight to any native destination, recent thread, or encrypted template with accent-insensitive search inside a FLAG_SECURE overlay.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>What ships in the current release</h2>
          <p>Focused daily workflows backed by strict local encryption and self-hosted multi-profile controls.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pillars-grid">
          <article class="pillar-card">
            <h3>1-tap QR pairing and profile hub</h3>
            <p>Scan or paste a single-use 5-minute <code>hermes://pair</code> link to connect a new phone in seconds, switch encrypted local profiles, and manage family or team invites in app.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar-card">
            <h3>First-profile admin console</h3>
            <p>The first profile on your server is admin by default with last-admin protection, user invitations, key rotation, active ticket revocation, and bounded per-profile concurrency caps.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar-card">
            <h3>Universal search and command palette</h3>
            <p>Search chats, notes, shared items, settings, and tools from the top bar on every screen, or press <code>Ctrl+K</code> to jump straight to any action or template inside a <code>FLAG_SECURE</code> overlay.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar-card">
            <h3>Everyday workflows and editable drafts</h3>
            <p>Use {{ curated_workflows_count }} built-in starters plus encrypted custom templates per profile. Voice dictation, cards, and workflows always stage an editable draft before sending.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar-card">
            <h3>Live connection doctor</h3>
            <p>Runs 6 parallel non-blocking health probes covering latency, <code>{{ expected_fork_capabilities }}/{{ expected_fork_capabilities }}</code> companion features, push, updates, permissions, and language sync with a redacted report copy.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar-card">
            <h3>Parallel multi-run and instant paging</h3>
            <p>Run concurrent tasks across multiple discussions for one user without canceling active streams or mixing deltas, backed by lazy history paging and bounded caches.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar-card">
            <h3>3 living workspaces and inline sharing</h3>
            <p>Work across Chats, Notes &amp; Tasks, and Apps with inline Shared filters, manage memory, skills, and appearance inside the top-bar Settings Hub, and share 7 resource kinds across profiles on the same server.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pillar-card">
            <h3>Verified signed updates</h3>
            <p>Check official GitHub Releases inside the app with constant-time SHA-256 verification and strict signing-certificate matching before handing off to Android’s installer.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-alt">
      <div class="container arch-split">
        <div>
          <h2>Fail-closed privacy from phone vault to server kernel</h2>
          <p>Every unlocked profile keeps its own Android Keystore AES-256-GCM vault, unlock backoff counter, active-run tracker, and widget scope. Locking or switching profiles wipes decoded caches, closes dialogs, and revokes in-flight callbacks immediately.</p>
          <p>On your Hermes server, each user lives in an isolated <code>/p/&lt;slug&gt;</code> SQLite WAL database while Linux kernel Landlock LSM prevents subprocesses from reading sibling profile directories. Closed-app push wakeups carry only opaque event IDs.</p>
          <div class="hero-cta">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="./docs/#security">Explore security model</a>
            <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="./docs/#multi-profile">Single-host setup</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="editorial-figure">
          <img src="../assets/marketing/privacy-architecture.png" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Three-column privacy and security architecture diagram showing Android Keystore AES-256-GCM vault, direct encrypted HTTPS and Tailscale link, and self-hosted Hermes server with isolated SQLite WAL and Linux kernel Landlock LSM">
          <figcaption>End-to-end boundary: on-device Keystore encryption, direct HTTPS or Tailscale transport with opaque push wakeups, and kernel-isolated server profiles.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>Light and dark themes on Android 16</h2>
          <p>Every screen adapts automatically to your chosen theme. Toggle Light or Dark in the top bar to switch the captures below live.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="editorial-figure figure-spacer">
          <img src="../assets/marketing/dual-theme-showcase-en.png" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Light paper and dark paper themes of Hermes Mobile side by side on Android 16 showing connection doctor, everyday workflows, command palette, and presence and appearance controls">
          <figcaption>Real Android 16 (1080x2340) captures side by side in warm paper light mode and low-glare dark mode.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="gallery-grid">
          <article class="capture-card" data-category="screen">
            <div class="capture-media is-phone">
              <img class="capture-phone-img" src="../assets/screens/en/command-palette.png" data-src-light="../assets/screens/en/command-palette.png" data-src-dark="../assets/screens/dark/en/command-palette.png" width="1080" height="2340" loading="lazy" alt="Global command palette quick jump overlay in English showing searchable actions, threads, and templates">
            </div>
            <div class="capture-body">
              <span class="badge">Android 16 · EN</span>
              <h3>Command palette (Ctrl+K)</h3>
              <p>Instant accent-insensitive jump across actions, recent discussions, and encrypted templates.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="capture-card" data-category="screen">
            <div class="capture-media is-phone">
              <img class="capture-phone-img" src="../assets/screens/en/templates.png" data-src-light="../assets/screens/en/templates.png" data-src-dark="../assets/screens/dark/en/templates.png" width="1080" height="2340" loading="lazy" alt="Everyday workflows panel in English with built-in starters and custom templates staging editable drafts">
            </div>
            <div class="capture-body">
              <span class="badge">Android 16 · EN</span>
              <h3>Everyday workflows</h3>
              <p>Built-in starters and encrypted personal templates that always stage editable drafts.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="capture-card" data-category="screen">
            <div class="capture-media is-phone">
              <img class="capture-phone-img" src="../assets/screens/en/connection-doctor.png" data-src-light="../assets/screens/en/connection-doctor.png" data-src-dark="../assets/screens/dark/en/connection-doctor.png" width="1080" height="2340" loading="lazy" alt="Live connection doctor panel in English verifying server latency, companion capabilities, push notifications, and updates">
            </div>
            <div class="capture-body">
              <span class="badge">Android 16 · EN</span>
              <h3>Connection doctor</h3>
              <p>Six parallel checks, companion capability verification, 1-tap fixes, and a safe redacted report.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="capture-card" data-category="screen">
            <div class="capture-media is-phone">
              <img class="capture-phone-img" src="../assets/screens/en/presence-control.png" data-src-light="../assets/screens/en/presence-control.png" data-src-dark="../assets/screens/dark/en/presence-control.png" width="1080" height="2340" loading="lazy" alt="Presence and look panel in English with all optional sharing switches off by default">
            </div>
            <div class="capture-body">
              <span class="badge">Android 16 · EN</span>
              <h3>Presence and look</h3>
              <p>Opt-in sharing controls all off by default, 1-tap full reset, and WCAG-AA day and night palettes.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="container footer-inner">
      <span>Hermes Mobile · Open source · Paper and teal design system</span>
      <div class="footer-links">
        <a href="./docs/">Documentation</a>
        <a href="./walkthrough/">Gallery</a>
        <a href="../fr/" data-lang-switch="fr" hreflang="fr" lang="fr">Version française</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/{{ repository }}" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        <a href="{{ fork_url }}" rel="noopener">Companion server</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script src="../assets/app.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
